From e419f6669cc741bbdb9a050606ee0865c37ac9b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joel Brower <joel.brower@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:22:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] build(android): add a Wails stand-in for the Android
 build

Wails v2 has no Android target. android/wailsshim is a drop-in module for
github.com/wailsapp/wails/v2 that mirrors the v2.16 API the desktop app uses,
so the app compiles unmodified. pkg/mobile carries calls, events and host
requests (pickers, dialogs, URLs, clipboard) across the bridge, with the same
argument and error conventions as Wails' own binding layer.

On a desktop OS, wails.Run serves the frontend with the Android shim and the
bridge over HTTP on the wails-dev port, as a browser harness for the exact
code the phone runs.

